    stage2_cranelift_direct_segv_nil_struct_fields_2026-08-24, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: built a full stage2 self-hosted Cranelift binary from the pre-fix tree; the doc's h2 probe did not SEGV on it (the nil-data shape is not live on a fresh Windows stage2 - the COFF/ELF SMF gate fires first, rc=1 fail-closed); the unguarded code shape WAS live: build_signature (cranelift_codegen_adapter.spl:435) derefs sig.params and sig.return_type.kind with no guard (backtrace B was already guarded at tip). Fix: fail-closed guard at build_signature top (sig == nil or params nil or return_type nil -> panic E-BACKEND-CRANELIFT-NIL-SIG, the module's existing panic idiom). Verification (child-process, SEGV-proof): forged-nil probe pre-fix rc=139 SEGV (captured by reverting my edit), post-fix stderr carries the diagnostic rc=127 on both jit and interpreter lanes; post-fix stage2 rebuilt from the shared cache (2 modules recompiled, 1794 reused) and re-probed - no SEGV; spec build_signature_nil_fields_fail_closed GREEN on the scratch seed. Residuals: the original h2.slf reduction can never print the diagnostic on a Windows stage2 (COFF/ELF gate first); the diagnostic path needs a Linux stage2 run (recipe documents); stage2 worker spawns die STATUS_DLL_INIT_FAILED when the stage2 binary is relocated (SCV admission pins sources to its exe-adjacent checkout root) - guard verification rests on the seed lanes which compile the same source; the full-tree check src/compiler could not complete on this host (check workers crash-loop 0xC0000142, environmental). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/70.backend/build_signature_nil_fields_fail_closed_spec.spl prevention=doc/07_guide/compiler/stage2_cranelift_nil_struct_fields_reverification.md"

